Don't feel stupid for not knowing that (but it's ok to feel stupid for
spelling dumb dum. <grin>).  Undead turning is from D&D. When an undead
monster was around, you could "turn" it.  I assume turn means "to divert
or deflect" and not "to rotate or revolve". The undead creature would flee
or be destroyed. I don't remember exactly, no-one every played a cleric in
my group.
So what nethack's turn undead spell / wand does is try to damage
the target undead monster and try to scare it.  Or if it hits an object
(or object in a monster's inventory) that is dead, it turns it so it isn't
dead anymore.  This doesn't make perfect sense, because it uses the exact
opposite mean of undead than what is expected. Also, it counts eggs as
dead objects. There is a prayer-like effect for knights and priests.

The biggest use early game, in my experience, is to revive a pet for
shoplifting.

